{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.SkeinMassRelation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.SkeinMassRelation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.predicted_ratio_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.predicted_ratio_pos","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L88-L94","doc":"The predicted ratio is positive when Vol(4₁) > 0 and q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.hbar_q_pos_of_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.hbar_q_pos_of_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L81-L86","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.agreement","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The prediction matches CODATA within uncertainty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.predicted_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.predicted_ratio","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L77-L77","doc":"The theoretical prediction: `m_μ/m_e = Vol(4₁)/ℏ_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.hbar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.hbar_q","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The quantum Planck constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.codata_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.codata_ratio","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L73-L73","doc":"CODATA muon-electron mass ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.vol_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.vol_pos","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Volume is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.vol_figure_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.vol_figure_eight","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the figure-eight knot 4₁.\n`Vol(4₁) = 2 · Cl₂(π/3) = 6 · Λ(π/3) ≈ 2.02988` — two regular ideal\ntetrahedra, each of volume `Cl₂(π/3) = 3 · Λ(π/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L65-L65","doc":"q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.q","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The substrate parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio.mk","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.LeptonMassRatio","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L54-L79","doc":"**Lepton mass ratio from knot volume**.\n\nThe muon-electron mass ratio is determined by the hyperbolic\nvolume of the figure-eight knot and the quantum Planck constant:\n`m_μ/m_e = Vol(4₁) / ℏ_q²`\nwhere `ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.skein_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.skein_mass","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The Skein relation for mass:\n`q · M(L₊) - q⁻¹ · M(L₋) = (q^(1/2) - q^(-1/2)) · M(L₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_zero","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Mass of smoothed resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_minus","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Mass of negative crossing resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mass_plus","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Mass of positive crossing resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L42-L42","doc":"q is greater than 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.q","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The substrate parameter q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.SkeinMassRelation","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/skein-mass-relation.lean#L32-L52","doc":"**Skein-mass relation**: the quantum Skein relation applied to\nthe mass functional.\n\nAt each crossing in the color-exchange space:\n`q · M(L₊) - q⁻¹ · M(L₋) = (q^{1/2} - q^{-1/2}) · M(L₀)` ","signatureChunk":0}]}